# Canonical Redis ACL entry for the inventory-v2 application user.
#
# Copy the `user` line below into `acl/users.acl` on the central Redis
# platform, replace <PASSWORD> with the real secret, replace <PREFIX> with the
# value of REDIS_KEY_PREFIX (WITHOUT the trailing colon — default
# "inventory-v2"), then run:
#
#   redis-cli -a "$REDIS_ADMIN_PASSWORD" ACL LOAD
#   redis-cli -a "$REDIS_ADMIN_PASSWORD" ACL GETUSER inventory-v2
#
# Both ACL axes are required and are INDEPENDENT of each other:
#   ~<PREFIX>:*            -> keys (cache, locks, BullMQ, rate limits)
#   &<PREFIX>:*            -> Pub/Sub channels for PUBLISH / SUBSCRIBE (glob)
#   &<PREFIX>:#/#*         -> EXACT pattern for root-namespace PSUBSCRIBE
#   &<PREFIX>:#/notifications#* -> EXACT pattern for the app namespace
#
# WHY THE EXACT PATTERNS ARE MANDATORY (Redis 7 src/acl.c):
#   "the pattern provided in PSUBSCRIBE can only be matched as a literal
#    against an ACL pattern (using plain string compare)"
# i.e. `is_pattern && !strcmp(pattern, channel)`. A single `&<PREFIX>:*` is
# enough for PUBLISH/SUBSCRIBE but NOT for `PSUBSCRIBE <PREFIX>:#/#*`, which
# is exactly what @socket.io/redis-adapter emits after RedisIoAdapter sets
# the adapter `key` option to `${REDIS_KEY_PREFIX}:`. Without the exact `&`
# grants Redis replies `NOPERM No permissions to access a channel`.
# Every new Socket.IO `namespace:` needs its own `&<PREFIX>:#<namespace>#*`
# entry; alternatively use `+allchannels`, which gives up channel isolation.
#
# +info is re-enabled after -@dangerous because ioredis' ready check calls
# INFO (otherwise it logs a warning on every connection). `+@all` covers
# BullMQ's EVAL/EVALSHA Lua scripts, streams, blocking pops and Pub/Sub;
# ioredis tolerates a denied CLIENT SETINFO silently. If your platform
# enforces a stricter command allowlist, keep at least @pubsub, @scripting,
# @blocking, @stream, @list, @sortedset, @hash, @set, @string, @keyspace,
# @read, @write, @slow and @connection, plus +info explicitly.
user inventory-v2 on ><PASSWORD> ~<PREFIX>:* &<PREFIX>:* &<PREFIX>:#/#* &<PREFIX>:#/notifications#* +@all -@admin -@dangerous +info
